- A genuine NVIDIA-hosted model investigation was recorded; exact event approval
  is separate. Current model selection/configuration and HTTP behavior should be
  traced through `src/config.ts`, `src/investigation/model.ts`,
  `src/investigation/nvidia.ts`, `src/http.ts` and `cli.ts` before editing.
- The earlier installation proof used an isolated source copy. Final release
  reproduction must use the actual submitted revision in a clean checkout.
- Full scenario evaluation, slides, sponsor explanation and demo remain release
  work. Do not infer completion from README text or earlier test totals.

Work required:
- Integrate Zayan's actual read-only inventory, billing, metrics, operations and
  dependency adapters behind the existing validated boundary as access permits.
  Verify account/region permissions, UTC periods, units/granularity, pagination,
  collection times, source authority and coverage. Jobs/dependencies may need
  operational sources outside native AWS APIs; unavailable authority must defer.
- Keep mock/fixture/live/stub provenance truthful per source and in reports.
  Review any required mixed-mode contract changes explicitly. Never relabel a
  synthetic observation as live or treat a generic connectivity probe as a full
  investigation/source proof. Record exact live coverage and remaining gaps.
- Verify the exact chosen model against current event/sponsor rules and actual
  access. Preserve the successful NVIDIA proof separately from eligibility.
  Document Cursor usage only from actual use, not the starter's expectations.
- Run a measured A/B/C/D and failure evaluation against a simple average-CPU
  heuristic. Report real denominators, disposition accuracy, unsafe positives,
